  "docs.qatt-hero.intro":
    "The opening section of a page: a rukun band on top, then a main heading, a short subtitle, two buttons and an optional install command, closed by a qatt band.",
  "docs.qatt-hero.usage":
    'Pass align="start" with media for a two-column hero: text at inline-start and the media in an arch frame at inline-end on large screens. Keep the subtitle to about 60 characters per line.',
  "docs.qatt-hero.rtl":
    "Columns follow the page direction, the primary button's arrow flips, and the install command is always shown left-to-right.",
  "docs.qatt-hero.a11y":
    "The title is the page's only h1. The animation is opt-in and stops under reduced motion, and the copy button announces “Copied”.",
  "docs.props.qatt-hero.eyebrow": "Short line above the title, shown in a badge.",
  "docs.props.qatt-hero.title": "Main heading, rendered as h1.",
  "docs.props.qatt-hero.subtitle": "Short description below the title.",
  "docs.props.qatt-hero.primaryCta":
    "Main button. A button with label, href and optional variant (qatt, default, outline or qatt-outline).",
  "docs.props.qatt-hero.secondaryCta":
    "Secondary button. A button with label, href and optional variant (qatt, default, outline or qatt-outline).",
  "docs.props.qatt-hero.install": "An install command shown left-to-right with a copy button, plus an optional label.",
  "docs.props.qatt-hero.motif": "Top band motif. Default rukun.",
  "docs.props.qatt-hero.align": "Content alignment: center (default) or start.",
  "docs.props.qatt-hero.media": "Image or element shown in an arch frame at inline-end on large screens.",
  "docs.props.qatt-hero.animate": "Paints the top band in; off under reduced motion.",
  "docs.majlis-welcome.intro":
    "A welcome section that receives visitors the way a guest is received. In the homes of Asir, the woman of the house gives the guest room special care and paints its walls with qatt together with her female relatives. This block draws on that spirit: a banat frieze on top, a warm heading and three welcome points.",
  "docs.majlis-welcome.usage":
    "Use it as the first thing people see after signing up, or as an introduction on your home page. Write like a host, not an advert: short sentences, plural address, and promises you keep.",
  "docs.majlis-welcome.rtl":
    "Media sits at inline-end on large screens, points read from inline-start, and the banat frieze is symmetric so it does not flip.",
  "docs.majlis-welcome.a11y":
    "The section is labelled by its heading, the points are a real list (ul), and the icons and frieze are hidden from assistive technology.",
  "docs.majlis-welcome.heritage":
    "Banat sprigs always stay plant-like: never add a dot or head above them, and never animate them in a way that suggests a figure. Do not attribute meanings to the motifs that no source documents.",
  "docs.majlis-welcome.copyNote":
    "If your copy mentions Al-Qatt Al-Asiri, say “inspired by” and stick to what is established: it is the art of Asiri women decorating the interior walls of their homes, especially guest rooms, and it was inscribed on UNESCO's Intangible Cultural Heritage list in 2017. Do not give a date for its origin; its origins are debated.",
  "docs.props.majlis-welcome.title": "Section heading; the section is labelled by it via aria-labelledby.",
  "docs.props.majlis-welcome.body": "Welcome text, one or two short paragraphs.",
  "docs.props.majlis-welcome.points": "Up to three welcome points, each with a title, body and optional icon.",
  "docs.props.majlis-welcome.media": "Image or element shown in an arch frame.",
  "docs.props.majlis-welcome.cta":
    "Optional call to action. A button with label, href and optional variant (qatt, default, outline or qatt-outline).",
  "docs.qatt-feature-grid.intro":
    "A grid of painted cards presenting your product's features, each with an icon in a coloured khatmah-like square, over a very faint shabakah background.",
  "docs.qatt-feature-grid.usage":
    "Three columns suit six features; two suit four. Keep each title to two or three words and the body to one sentence. Giving a feature an href makes the whole card clickable through a single inner link.",
  "docs.qatt-feature-grid.rtl": "The grid fills from inline-start; only directional icons flip.",
  "docs.qatt-feature-grid.a11y":
    "Feature titles are h3 under the section heading; icons are decorative. A clickable card has one link, named by the feature title.",
